00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:56.640
Experts say always-listening AI gadgets could land wearers in legal trouble.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.210
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.170
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.510
Machines: Sam Altman says OpenAI will build a humanoid robot,

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.480
with a cool demo in 2027.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.290
In China, a 4-metre robot called Neo1 can lift more than 500 kilos.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.930
And in Korea, a robot lab now makes drug candidates around the clock, unmanned.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.090
AI learned teamwork. The future's a group project, so let's be good teammates.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.040
Every day, the curve gets steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.510
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.530
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.910
This has been the singularity, one day at a time.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.870
Feel the SI.

